traceability.evidence:
Test execution: `npm test -- --runInBand --verbose` ran all suites successfully. Output includes: - PASS tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts - "Auto-fix behavior (Story 008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX)" - Covers [REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING], [REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT], [REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE], [REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE]. - All 39 test suites and 299 tests passed.,Story-specific tests: tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts - File header explicitly ties tests to story and requirements: - `@story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md` - `@req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING` - `@req REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT` - `@supports docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT` - REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING: - Valid cases ensure already-annotated functions/methods unchanged. - Invalid cases verify `--fix` adds `@story` for: - plain FunctionDeclaration - FunctionExpression assigned to const - class MethodDefinition - TS `declare function` - TS interface `TSMethodSignature` - Template configurability: - Test "[REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE] uses configured templates for functions and methods" asserts custom `annotationTemplate` and `methodAnnotationTemplate` produce expected outputs. - Selective auto-fix: - Test "[REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE] does not insert annotations when autoFix is false" asserts `output: null` while still reporting an error. - REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT: - Tests under "valid-annotation-format --fix simple @story extension issues" verify: - Already-correct `.story.md` path unchanged. - `.story` → `.story.md`. - bare path (no extension) → `.story.md`. - REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE: - Test "does not apply suffix fix when autoFix is false" asserts `output: null` while still reporting `invalidStoryFormat`.,Implementation of REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING / TEMPLATE / SELECTIVE: - src/rules/require-story-annotation.ts - `meta.fixable = "code"` enables ESLint auto-fix. - Options schema includes: - `annotationTemplate: { type: "string" }` - `methodAnnotationTemplate: { type: "string" }` - `autoFix: { type: "boolean" }` - `create(context)` derives: - `annotationTemplate`, `methodAnnotationTemplate` (trimmed, optional) - `autoFix` defaulting to `true` when not explicitly false. - Passes these through to visitor builder: `buildVisitors(context, sourceCode, { ..., annotationTemplate, methodAnnotationTemplate, autoFix })`. - src/rules/helpers/require-story-helpers.ts - REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE: - `getAnnotationTemplate(override)` returns trimmed override if non-empty; otherwise returns the built-in template: ``/** @story ${STORY_PATH} */`` where `STORY_PATH` is the canonical story path. - `buildTemplateConfig(options)` returns `{ effectiveTemplate, allowFix }` based on `annotationTemplateOverride` and `autoFixToggle`. - REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE: - `shouldApplyAutoFix(autoFix)` → `false` only when explicitly `false`; otherwise `true`. - `reportMissing` calls `coreReportMissing` with injected deps including `buildTemplateConfig`, `createAddStoryFix`, etc. - `reportMethod` similarly injects `getAnnotationTemplate`, `shouldApplyAutoFix`, `createMethodFix`. - src/rules/helpers/require-story-core.ts - REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING / SAFE / PRESERVE: - `createAddStoryFix(target, annotationTemplate)`: - Computes insertion position with `getInsertionStart(target)` (using AST `range` and handling export declarations). - Returns a fixer that does `fixer.insertTextBeforeRange([start, start], `${annotationTemplate}
`)` — inserts only a new comment line before the node, no code changes. - `createMethodFix(node, annotationTemplate)`: - Similar logic but inserts `${annotationTemplate}
 ` to maintain indentation before method body. - `DEFAULT_SCOPE` includes `FunctionDeclaration`, `FunctionExpression`, `MethodDefinition`, `TSMethodSignature`, `TSDeclareFunction`, matching the test coverage.,Visitor wiring and rule behavior (integration & UX consistency): - src/rules/helpers/require-story-visitors.ts - Each visitor (`FunctionDeclaration`, `FunctionExpression`, `ArrowFunctionExpression`, `TSDeclareFunction`, `TSMethodSignature`, `MethodDefinition`) calls `helperReportMissing` or `helperReportMethod` only when `options.shouldProcessNode(node)` is true, ensuring consistency with scope/exportPriority. - For each report, passes: - `annotationTemplateOverride: options.annotationTemplate` or `options.methodAnnotationTemplate ?? options.annotationTemplate`. - `autoFixToggle: options.autoFix`. - This ensures all function-like patterns share the same templating and autoFix semantics, satisfying consistent, predictable UX (AC: User Experience).,Implementation of REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT / SAFE / PRESERVE / SELECTIVE: - src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts - `meta.fixable = "code"` with a docstring explicitly tying fixability to Story 008.0 and limiting fixes to safe suffix normalization. - Options schema from `getRuleSchema()` includes `autoFix: { type: "boolean" }`. - `create(context)` resolves options via `resolveOptions(context.options || [])` which returns a `ResolvedAnnotationOptions` with `autoFix` boolean. - Program visitor traverses all comments and calls `processComment`, which ultimately calls `finalizePendingAnnotation` for `@story`/`@req` and `validateImplementsAnnotation` for `@supports`. - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-options.ts - `AnnotationRuleOptions` includes `autoFix?: boolean` with comment: "Global toggle for auto-fix behavior ... When false, no automatic suffix-normalization fixes are applied." - `resolveAutoFixFlag` ensures `autoFix` defaults to `true` unless explicitly set `false`. - `resolveOptions` stores resolved defaults (including `autoFix`) for other helpers. - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-utils.ts - `getFixedStoryPath(original)` implements suffix-only normalization: - Returns `null` when path contains `".."` (satisfies REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE: avoids traversal changes). - Returns `null` when path already ends with `.story.md` (no-op). - `.story` → `.story.md`. - `.md` → `.story.md`. - No extension → `.story.md`. - All transformations return modified strings without touching directories or anything outside the suffix. - This function is used only for `@story` paths, not for `@req`, satisfying REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT scope. - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-validators.ts - `validateStoryAnnotation(context, comment, rawValue, options)`: - For missing values: reports `invalidStoryFormat` with a detailed message (no fix), satisfying error clarity. - If `pathPattern.test(collapsed)` is true, accepts without fix. - If internal whitespace exists (`/\s/.test(trimmed)`), it calls `reportInvalidStoryFormat` (no fix) — protects against ambiguous values. - Computes `fixed = getFixedStoryPath(collapsed)`. - If `fixed` exists and `pathPattern.test(fixed)`: - When `options.autoFix !== false`, calls `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix(...)`, which: - Uses `createStoryFix` to compute a precise `replaceTextRange` within the comment text (only the path, preserving other comment text and whitespace). - When `options.autoFix === false`, falls back to `reportInvalidStoryFormat` (no fix), satisfying REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE. - If `fixed` is `null` or not pattern-compliant, calls `reportInvalidStoryFormat` (no fix), satisfying REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE and REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE for unfixable/ambiguous cases. - `createStoryFix(context, comment, fixed)`: - Locates `@story` occurrence in the original comment via `commentText.indexOf("@story")`. - Uses regex `rest.match(/[^\S
]*([^
*]+)/)` to capture just the value segment, and computes an exact `fixRange` inside `comment.range`. - Returns `null` if the tag or value segment cannot be located, ensuring no partial or dangerous replacements. - `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix` uses `createStoryFix`, and explicitly falls back to non-fix reporting when `fixFactory` is `null`. - Together, these satisfy REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE and REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE: - Fixes apply only to the `@story` path text. - No changes to surrounding code, comments, or whitespace beyond the replaced substring. - Tests in tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts validate: - .story → .story.md (`"adds .md extension for .story path"`). - bare path → .story.md (`"adds .story.md extension when missing entirely"`). - When `autoFix: false`, `output: null` while still reporting `invalidStoryFormat`.,Acceptance Criteria mapping: - Core Functionality (ESLint --fix resolves common violations): - require-story-annotation: meta.fixable = "code" and rule visitors wired with fixer; tests show `RuleTester` expects specific `output` when running the rule (which simulates ESLint `--fix`). - valid-annotation-format: meta.fixable = "code", suffix-only fix logic in `validateStoryAnnotation` and `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix`; tested via RuleTester. - Quality Standards (safe, preserve behavior/formatting): - For missing `@story`: - createAddStoryFix / createMethodFix only insert comments before nodes; they never alter existing code text. - Template is a single-line JSDoc; tests confirm code body remains identical aside from added comment. - For path format fixes: - getFixedStoryPath limits changes to suffix and rejects paths with `".."`. - createStoryFix restricts replacement to the story-value substring; no reflowing or reformatting. - Integration (works with existing rules and ESLint toolchain): - require-story-annotation and valid-annotation-format are part of the plugin’s exported rules (verified indirectly via tests such as tests/plugin-default-export-and-configs.test.ts and tests/config/eslint-config-validation.test.ts which all passed in the Jest run). - Both rules use ESLint’s standard RuleModule interface and are exercised through `RuleTester`, proving compatibility with ESLint’s core toolchain. - User Experience (consistent & predictable fixes): - require-story-annotation auto-fix covers multiple node types consistently, governed by shared helpers and configuration. - Tests show annotated functions & methods are left unchanged; only missing cases receive fixes. - valid-annotation-format’s behavior is deterministic: either no-op, safe suffix normalization (when unambiguous), or diagnostic-only when ambiguous, enforced by tests. - Error Handling (graceful when auto-fix not safe): - getFixedStoryPath returns `null` for unsafe cases (e.g., `".."`), leading to non-fix diagnostics only. - createStoryFix returns `null` when it cannot reliably find the value range; reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix then falls back to `reportInvalidStoryFormat`. - For `autoFix: false` configurations, validateStoryAnnotation still reports errors without applying auto-fix (covered by tests in auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts). - Documentation (user-facing description of auto-fix capabilities): - user-docs/api-reference.md - Section "traceability/require-story-annotation": - Explicitly describes `--fix` inserting a placeholder JSDoc @story above functions/methods/TS declarations. - Documents `annotationTemplate`, `methodAnnotationTemplate`, and `autoFix` options and their behavior, aligning with REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE and REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE. - Section "traceability/valid-annotation-format": - Explains that in `--fix` mode only safe `@story` path suffix normalization is performed (e.g., adding `.md` or `.story.md`). - States that no directory or base-name inference occurs and that `autoFix` controls whether these suffix fixes are applied. - Both sections provide clear, example-based descriptions of what gets fixed and under which constraints, satisfying the Documentation acceptance criterion.
